          ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $C$ is upper triangular: **True.** All the entries below the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is lower triangular: **True.** All the entries above the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **True.** All the entries below the main diagonal of ${C}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $C$ is upper triangular.\n- $C$ is lower triangular.\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular."
