          ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **False.** This fails because $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **True.** This holds because the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nA+{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular."
