          ":question/id": "814b1f0e-0432-56a4-8a3b-10efb7462756",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-126474",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $B$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular: **False.** This fails because $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${B}^{T}+B$ is upper triangular: **True.** This holds because the result of ${B}^{T}+B$ has all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}+B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- ${B}^{T}+B$ is upper triangular."
