              ":question/id": "fe3edf12-af5b-5bb0-b5b3-efb6cd809134",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4394",
              ":question/problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} \\\\ 6 & -1 & {\\color{blue}0} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: $a_{21}=6 \\neq 0.$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Describing a Triangular Matrix"
          },
          {
